[2026-03-15T00:15:43.065Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012SdwNoDCAJmS6PBvDVUiVS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It handles recording, uploading, and managing replays through command-line interface.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n1. Navigate to https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Set the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Upload:**\n- `replayio record [url]` - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` - Upload recordings (interactive menu if no IDs specified)\n\n**Management:**\n- `replayio list` - View all local recordings with metadata\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` - Delete recordings (use `-a` flag for all)\n- `replayio login/logout` - Authentication management\n\n**Other:**\n- `replayio info` - Display CLI and browser version info\n- `replayio update` - Update Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>` - Upload source maps with grouping options\n\n## Common Workflow\nRecord a session, review it locally, then upload using the recording ID. The tool returns a viewable URL after successful upload.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99c20f83-7864-4a55-a0d6-29119d896fad","uuid":"139a280c-17a1-4fc8-a81a-ebbce1704711","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It handles recording, uploading, and managing replays through command-line interface.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n1. Navigate to https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Set the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Upload:**\n- `replayio record [url]` - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` - Upload recordings (interactive menu if no IDs specified)\n\n**Management:**\n- `replayio list` - View all local recordings with metadata\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` - Delete recordings (use `-a` flag for all)\n- `replayio login/logout` - Authentication management\n\n**Other:**\n- `replayio info` - Display CLI and browser version info\n- `replayio update` - Update Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>` - Upload source maps with grouping options\n\n## Common Workflow\nRecord a session, review it locally, then upload using the recording ID. The tool returns a viewable URL after successful upload.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options.","durationMs":3785,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T00:15:43.938Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kq4Nmn71ZyEhvYbsN2sx7w","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** A tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings that \"perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Primary Function:** Replay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by exploring application behavior through time-based analysis.\n\n**Core Methodology:** The documentation emphasizes a structured approach—frame questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Exploratory Tools:**\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (find, read, and search JS files with execution hit counts)\n\n**Explanatory Tools:**\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control dependencies showing what triggered execution)\n- State details (point descriptions, DOM element inspection, React component trees, expressions)\n\n**Key Insight:** The guidance recommends identifying relevant code, verifying execution, and using the Logpoint tool to \"see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to spot anomalies and investigate further.\n\nThis skill transforms recordings into queryable databases of execution events, enabling precise answers about application behavior."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99c20f83-7864-4a55-a0d6-29119d896fad","uuid":"bbc85d0b-85da-425c-86f9-22570ecc79d8","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** A tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings that \"perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Primary Function:** Replay MCP enables investigation of browser recordings by exploring application behavior through time-based analysis.\n\n**Core Methodology:** The documentation emphasizes a structured approach—frame questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, employ explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Exploratory Tools:**\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, storage access, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (find, read, and search JS files with execution hit counts)\n\n**Explanatory Tools:**\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control dependencies showing what triggered execution)\n- State details (point descriptions, DOM element inspection, React component trees, expressions)\n\n**Key Insight:** The guidance recommends identifying relevant code, verifying execution, and using the Logpoint tool to \"see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to spot anomalies and investigate further.\n\nThis skill transforms recordings into queryable databases of execution events, enabling precise answers about application behavior.","durationMs":4152,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
